0..83 Comment "/// This source calls recursions staged past their first parameter at named values."
84..87 Comment "///"
88..162 Comment "/// It pins how the kernel unfolds a constant at a staged fixpoint\'s gate."
163..166 Comment "///"
167..540 Comment "/// `le` recurses under a case on its second parameter, so the lowering stages its fixpoint there. The fixpoint takes the first parameter as a leading argument. Called at a named value, the fixpoint sticks at its gate on the name. The checker unfolds the name there, and the kernel replays that unfolding at the staged argument, past the leading one, before the gate opens."
541..544 Comment "///"
